    "created_at": "2023-02-24T15:11:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-02-24T15:11:16Z",
    "body": "I guess if the user drops the same set of files as the current set, I'd expect either (a) a cancel event or (b) no events at all to fire at that time.  Firing an input and a change event when the files didn't change exposes (I think) that the action was drag/drop rather than via the picker.  (Also, for the file picker case, Chromium, at least, fires the input and the change events at the same time, after the user has closed the picker.)\r\n\r\n(Also, for the picker case, I don't recall if there are currently APIs that allow the *page* to open the file picker, but if there are, that's a good reason that a `cancel` event should be exposed.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
